From 5cb9dee7189862e711873952d4f5b88ea4d4dba3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Bernhard M. Wiedemann" <bwiedemann@suse.de>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:48:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Port the staff finders to Python 3 integer semantics

Python 2 "/" on ints floored; Python 3 returns floats, which break list
indexing/slicing and Int() plugin arguments.  Use "//" wherever the
Python 2 code relied on integer division, so results match Python 2:

- stafffinder_projections: staff break, peak and low-pass window
  indices; __get_peakheight's window is ypos +/- (staffline_height//2)//2
  as before.
- stafffinder_miyao: merging two anchor points on one scanline made
  their y a float, which later reaches miyao_find_edge(Int y) and the
  StafflinePolygon vertices; also the debug marker sizes.
- stafffinder_dalitz: replace dict.has_key/iteritems.

The Dalitz finder still needs its C++ plugin (get_staff_skeleton_list),
which is not part of this tree; projections and Miyao work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_dalitz.py     |  4 ++--
 .../toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_miyao.py      |  6 +++---
 .../musicstaves/stafffinder_projections.py         | 14 +++++++-------
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/musicstaves/gamera/toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_dalitz.py b/musicstaves/gamera/toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_dalitz.py
index 0881e34..dab1e26 100644
--- a/musicstaves/gamera/toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_dalitz.py
+++ b/musicstaves/gamera/toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_dalitz.py
@@ -426,13 +426,13 @@ processing.
             for g in groups:
                 if g.col_end - g.col_start + 1 > max_group_width / 2:
                     n = g.max_line - g.min_line + 1
-                    if num_hist.has_key(n):
+                    if n in num_hist:
                         num_hist[n] += 1
                     else:
                         num_hist[n] = 1
             max_count = 0
             estimated_num_lines = 0
-            for (n,c) in num_hist.iteritems():
+            for (n,c) in num_hist.items():
                 if c > max_count:
                     estimated_num_lines = n
                     max_count = c
diff --git a/musicstaves/gamera/toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_miyao.py b/musicstaves/gamera/toolkits/musicstaves/stafffinder_miyao.py
